    <DataNode elementId="CPD-17595" textLabel="(-)-yatein" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="GMLDZDDTZKXJLU-JKSUJKDBSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="780" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xu, O-28, hartmut">The lignan |FRAME:CPD-17595| is a typical component of heartwood in angiosperm trees |CITS:[Erdtman79]| that serves as long-term protectant against pathogen attacks and significantly contributes to the robustness, hence lifespan, of the trees |CITS:[20371107]|. In addition, yatein is a key intermediate in the formation of |FRAME:CPD-8959| and its derivatives (see |FRAME: PWY-7749|), which are important precursors for anti-cancer drugs such as |FRAME:CPD-16754|, |FRAME:CPD-16755| and |FRAME:CPD-17609| |CITS:[Umezawa03][15378293]|.</Comment>
